  "body": "[Secondary browser contexts](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#secondary-browsing-context) seem to not be implemented by browsers other than Firefox with `rel=\"sidebar\"` links.\n\n[window.sidebar](https://www.fxsitecompat.com/en-CA/docs/2015/window-sidebar-will-be-removed/) is planned to be removed which appears to be the only public API to such a secondary context.\n\nFrom the tests that I have done it seems that all browsers besides Firefox treat links with `rel=\"sidebar\"` as a normal link. This appears not to have changed in situation since 2009: https://blog.whatwg.org/the-road-to-html-5-link-relations#rel-sidebar\n\nSo if there are no implementers interested and it seems to make sense to remove it.\n",
